// Season cycle (SAD-P2 §3, §7). Season n uses row n % len; worldgen uses row 0.
// air_temp: clamp for surface and sky-open air, water and ice, in 0.1 °C.
// rain: per-column amount each sub-step, scaled by the seeded pattern (/256),
// so a column gets about (rain - 1) / 2 per sub-step (1 or less: none). Kept
// near what ponds evaporate and vent (eco.ron evap_table), so the world does
// not flood over the seasons (playtest A1: rain 64-160 flooded it). Winter is
// dry: rain on ice stays ice into spring and keeps the ponds from drying.
(
    substeps: 8,
    seasons: [
        (key: "spring", air_temp: 100, rain: 8),
        (key: "summer", air_temp: 220, rain: 6),
        (key: "autumn", air_temp: 80, rain: 10),
        (key: "winter", air_temp: -80, rain: 0),
    ],
)
